  "image_tag": "bench-toolz",
  "instruction": "## Goal\n\nAdd a new public `apply` function that calls a function with given arguments, and expose it in the `toolz.curried` namespace so callers can invoke functions in a curried/functional style.\n\n## Observable behavior\n\n```python\nimport toolz.functoolz as ft\napply = getattr(ft, 'apply', None)\nassert apply is not None\nassert apply(double, 5) == 10\nassert tuple(map(apply, [double, inc, double], [10, 500, 8000])) == (20, 501, 16000)\nassert raises(TypeError, apply)\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- The `apply` function must be public and importable from `toolz.functoolz`.\n- The `apply` function must also be available in the `toolz.curried` namespace.\n- Do not modify or remove any existing public APIs.\n- Only files in scope may be changed: `toolz/__init__.py`, `toolz/_signatures.py`, `toolz/curried/__init__.py`, `toolz/curried/operator.py`, `toolz/functoolz.py`, `toolz/tests/test_functoolz.py`.\n\n## How success is measured\n\nRun the verifier command:\n\n```bash\npython -m pytest -q toolz/tests/test_functoolz.py::test_apply\n```\n\nThe test must pass.",
